<h1>XML Templates for Custom PDF Reports</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><a href="Custom_Report_Generation.htm">Custom PDF Reports</a> in KUBE use XML template files for definition of the graphic and text elements in the report pages as well as the page properties (size, orientation, page numbers, etc.)</p>
<h2>Coordinate system</h2>
<p>Origin of the coordinate system is in the top-left corner of the page and is independent from page orientation. Positive X is to the right, positive Y is to the bottom.</p>
<p><img src="../Images/page_coord_system.gif" width="281px" height="194px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<h2>XML Template Structure</h2>
<p>XML template consists of header and drawing object definition enclosed in the <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">form</span> tag. Name of the object is with first uppercase letter and its attributes are all defined in lowercase letters.</p>
<p class="Code">&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-16" standalone="yes"?&gt;<br>
&lt;form&gt;<br>
&lt;Object1 ... /&gt;<br>
&lt;Object2 ... /&gt;<br>
.........<br>
&lt;ObjectN ... /&gt;<br>
&lt;/form&gt;</p>
<p>Objects can be used in the following two ways:</p>
<ol type="1" class="whs5">
<li class="kadov-p">
<p>Short form: <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">&lt;</span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-weight:bold;"><b>Object</b></span> <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-style:italic;"><i>attribute_1</i></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">="value1"</span> <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-style:italic;"><i>attribute_2</i></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">="value_2" ...</span> <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-style:italic;"><i>attribute_N</i></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">="value_N"/&gt;</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p">
<p>Long form: <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">&lt;</span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-weight:bold;"><b>Object</b></span> <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-style:italic;"><i>attribute_1</i></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">="value1"</span> <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-style:italic;"><i>attribute_2</i></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">="value_2" ...</span> <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-style:italic;"><i>attribute_N</i></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">="value_N"&gt;content&lt;/</span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; font-weight:bold;"><b>Object</b></span><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">&gt;</span><br>
In this case the <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">content</span> is omitted by KUBE and the expression is equivalent to this of the short form.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="sub-head">Header</p>
<p>The header consists of the following tree attributes:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>version</b></span> - should be always <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>1.0</i></span>.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>encoding</b></span> - use the proper encoding for the character set used for text contents and variable names and contents.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>The following list contains the supported encodings:</p>
<p>For ANSI XML files:</p>
<p class="Code">UTF-8<br>
UNICODE-1-1-UTF-8<br>
UNICODE-2-0-UTF-8<br>
US-ASCII<br>
ISO-8859-1<br>
ISO-8859-2<br>
ISO-8859-4<br>
ISO-8859-5<br>
ISO-8859-6<br>
ISO-8859-7<br>
ISO-8859-8<br>
ISO-8859-9<br>
WINDOWS-1250<br>
WINDOWS-1251<br>
WINDOWS-1252<br>
WINDOWS-1253<br>
WINDOWS-1254<br>
WINDOWS-1255<br>
WINDOWS-1256<br>
WINDOWS-1257<br>
WINDOWS-1258</p>
<p>For Unicode XML files:</p>
<p class="Code">UTF-16<br>
ISO-10646-UCS-2<br>
UNICODE-2-0-UTF-16</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>standalone</b></span> - should be always <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>yes</i></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CImportant">
<p class="Important">All attribute values (strings enclosed in double quotes) in XML template are case sensitive. This means that, for example, <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">orientation="Landscape"</span> or <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">orientation="LANDSCAPE"</span> are not equal to <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">orientation="landscape"</span>. Use the proper values for attributes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p3"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Notes:</b></span> If you create the XML template manually, i.e. in a text editor, in attribute values always replace the following characters: <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;</b></span> (ampersand), <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&lt;</b></span> (less-than sign), <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&gt;</b></span> (greater-than sign), <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span> (apostrophe), and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>"</b></span> (quotation mark) with <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;amp;</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;lt;</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;gt;</b></span>, <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;apos;</b></span>, and <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;quot;</b></span>. If the text editor is non-Unicode and you want to insert character that is not in the character set from the current code page, use the following form: <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;#N;</b></span>, where N is the Unicode for the character in decimal (base 10), or <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;#xN;</b></span>, where N is the Unicode for the character in hexadecimal (base 16).<br>
For example:<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
&amp;#38;</b></span> - ampersand <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&amp;</b></span> (in decimal)<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
&amp;#xA9;</b></span> - copyright sign <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>©</b></span> (in hexadecimal)<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
&amp;#169;</b></span> - copyright sign <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>©</b></span> (in decimal)<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><br>
&amp;#x2122;</b></span> - trade mark sign <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>"</b></span> (in hexadecimal)</p>
<p>For more information about XML specification, please refer to the World Wide Web Consortium XML homepage at <a href="http://www.w3.org/XML/">http://www.w3.org/XML/</a>.</p>
<h2 class="whs6">Objects Description</h2>
<p>Currently the following drawing objects are supported by KUBE:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">Page</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">PageVariable</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">MainImage</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">Image</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">PageNumber</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">Text</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">Variable</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">Box</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-style:normal;">Line</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>The following is a description of each of them.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Page</p>
<p><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Page</i></span> object defines the page properties. It should appear only once in the template.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>unit</b></span> defines measuring units for all objects can be <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>mm</i></span> or <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>inch</i></span>.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>size</b></span> defines page size. Commonly used types are:</p>
</li>
</ul>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs7">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
<td bgcolor="#808080" class="whs9">
<p align="center" class="whs10">Code</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#808080" class="whs11">
<p align="center" class="whs10">Page Type</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
<td bgcolor="#FFFFC1" class="whs12">
<p class="whs13">1</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#FFFFC1" class="whs14">
<p class="whs15">Letter</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
<td bgcolor="#FFFF00" class="whs16">
<p class="whs13">5</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#FFFF00" class="whs17">
<p class="whs15">Legal</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
<td bgcolor="#FFFFC1" class="whs12">
<p class="whs13">9</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#FFFFC1" class="whs14">
<p class="whs15">A4</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
<td bgcolor="#FFFF00" class="whs16">
<p class="whs13">8</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#FFFF00" class="whs17">
<p class="whs15">A3</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
<td bgcolor="#FFFFC1" class="whs12">
<p class="whs13">66</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#FFFFC1" class="whs14">
<p class="whs15">A2</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>Supported sizes are 124. Complete list of size codes is given in <a href="Appendix_A_Inspection.htm">Appendix A</a>.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:bold;">orientation <span style="font-weight:normal;">defines page orientation can be</span> <span style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;"><i>landscape</i></span> <span style="font-weight:normal;">or</span> <span style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;"><i>portrait</i></span><span style="font-weight:normal;">.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note:</b></span> "portrait" value leaves the page as its initial size, while "landscape" value rotates the page to 90 degrees, i.e. swaps width and height. If this attribute is absent then it assumes that it is "landscape".<br>
For example:<br>
1. If size="9" (A4 - 210mm x 297mm) and orientation="portrait", this will make the page size 210mm x 297mm.<br>
2. If size="9" (A4 - 210mm x 297mm) and orientation="landscape", this will make the page size 297mm x 210mm.<br>
3. If size="77" (A4 Rotated - 297mm x 210mm) and orientation="portrait", this will make the page size 297mm x 210mm.<br>
4. If size="77" (A4 Rotated - 297mm x 210mm) and orientation="landscape", this will make the page size 210mm x 297mm.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-weight:bold;">offsetx, offsety <span style="font-weight:normal;">defines origin offset. It will offset all of the object with given offsetx and offsety use these attributes to place all of the drawn objects inside printable area. If these attributes are absent, there will be no offset.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example">Example:</p>
<p class="Example">&lt;Page unit="mm" size="9" orientation="landscape" offsetx="5" offsety="5"/&gt;</p>
<p>We are using A4 paper, landcape (297 x 210 mm), all units are in mm, origin moved 5mm down and 5 mm left.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">PageVariable</p>
<p><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> object defines placement, size, and name of the page that is to be included in the report page(s). This object has a name and its name and contents (the page name) will be displayed in Step 1 of <a href="Custom_Report_Generation.htm">Custom PDF Report</a> Wizard. The page name can be changed from there. Can used as many <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>PageVariable</i></span> objects as needed.</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>x, y</b></span> top-left corner of placement rectangle.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>width, height</b></span> width and height of placement rectangle.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>name</b></span> name of the variable. Will be displayed in the first column of the table from Step 1 of the Custom PDF Report Wizard.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>contents</b></span> text to be displayed. Will be displayed in the second column of the table from Step 1 of the Custom PDF Report Wizard.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Example">Example:</p>
<p class="Example"><span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">&lt;PageVariable x="30" y="20" width="120" height="80" name="TopLeft"</span> <span style="margin-left:40px; font-family:'Courier New' , monospace; text-align:left;">contents="New page 1"/&gt;</span></p>
<p>Page thumbnail will be placed in the rectangle (30; 20) (150; 100). Also in the table from Step 1 of the wizard this will appear like the following:</p>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs7">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs8">
